  DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.

  Only the release line, end-of-life date, LTS date and latest release are copied. The product
  descriptions on endoflife.date (derived from Wikipedia, CC BY-SA 3.0) are not copied.
  The snapshot records its own fetch date in the "fetchedAt" field.

Node.js LTS codenames (the "codename" field of the Node.js lines in data/eol.json)

  Source: https://nodejs.org/download/release/index.json (the official Node.js release index).
  Only the pairs "major version -> LTS codename" are taken. Node.js is MIT-licensed,
  Copyright Node.js contributors. No separate terms page was found for the index itself.
  If the index cannot be read when the snapshot is refreshed, the previous pairs are kept.

